From 0c3385e5a9695466f86205a62b2e1efa36e7e856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Silt <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:14:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: serve _session/steering and _claude/background_tasks on
 ACP v2

The v2 core now registers _session/steering with v1's wire contract, and
advertises it as the top-level initialize _meta.steering. A steer while a
turn is open pushes the message into Claude Code's streaming input at
priority now, or later while a permission request or elicitation of the
session or a subagent awaits the user. With no running turn it answers
promptRequired when the request opts in, else sends the content as a
session/prompt and answers startedNewTurn once Claude Code takes it in.
The request types and parser move from src/v1/steering.ts to the shared
src/steering.ts.

_claude/background_tasks ({sessionId, toolCallId?} -> {backgrounded})
calls Claude Code's Query.backgroundTasks, and is advertised as the
top-level initialize _meta.claudeCode.backgroundTasks.
