+
+Both versions serve `_session/steering`, advertised as the top-level `_meta.steering` of the
+`initialize` response: it injects a message into the running turn. v2 also serves
+`_claude/background_tasks` (`{sessionId, toolCallId?}` → `{backgrounded}`), advertised as the
+top-level `_meta.claudeCode.backgroundTasks`: it moves the foreground Bash commands and subagents,
+or the one task that the tool call started, to the background, as Ctrl+B does in Claude Code.
 
 `session/prompt` takes an `idempotencyKey`: a prompt that a client sends again with the same key
